# Incremental Static Regeneration (ISR) in Next.js

**ISR** allows updating static pages in the background *without needing to rebuild the entire website*.

```typescript
// Revalidate page data at most every 60 seconds
export const revalidate = 60;
```

# Next.js Route Handlers (`route.ts`)

Route handlers allow creating custom HTTP endpoints using Web standard `Request` and `Response` objects:

```typescript
import { NextRequest, NextResponse } from "next/server";

export async function GET(req: NextRequest) {
  return NextResponse.json({ status: "healthy" });
}

export async function POST(req: NextRequest) {
  const body = await req.json();
  return NextResponse.json({ received: body }, { status: 201 });
}
```

# Implementing Pagination in Next.js

Use **URL Search Parameters** (`?page=2&limit=20`) in Server Components:

```typescript
export default async function ProductsPage({
  searchParams,
}: {
  searchParams: Promise<{ page?: string }>;
}) {
  const { page = "1" } = await searchParams;
  const data = await fetchProducts(Number(page));
  return <ProductList items={data} />;
}
```
